# 中频词汇 List10
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List10核心词汇

{{install}}{/ɪnˈstɔːl/}{安装；设置}{The company installed solar panels on the roof.}}
{{instinct}}{/ˈɪstɪŋkt/}{本能；直觉}{Her instinct told her something was wrong.}}
{{institute}}{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt/}{机构；设立}{The government instituted new safety regulations.}}
{{integrate}}{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/}{整合；融入}{The school works to integrate technology into the curriculum.}}
{{integrity}}{/ɪnˈteɡrəti/}{正直；完整性}{The company is known for its integrity and transparency.}}
{{intense}}{/ɪnˈtens/}{强烈的；紧张的}{The competition for the award was intense.}}
{{interact}}{/ˌɪntərˈækt/}{互动；相互作用}{Visitors can interact with the exhibits at the museum.}}
{{interface}}{/ˈɪntəfeɪs/}{界面；接口}{The user interface is intuitive and easy to navigate.}}
{{internal}}{/ɪnˈtɜːnl/}{内部的；国内的}{The company conducted an internal investigation.}}
{{interpret}}{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt/}{解释；翻译}{The data can be interpreted in several ways.}}
{{intervene}}{/ˌɪntəˈviːn/}{干预；介入}{The court intervened to protect the rights of the workers.}}
{{intimate}}{/ˈɪntɪmət/}{亲密的；私人的}{The restaurant has an intimate and romantic atmosphere.}}
{{intricate}}{/ˈɪntrɪkət/}{错综复杂的}{The mechanism is incredibly intricate and precise.}}
{{intrinsic}}{/ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk/}{内在的；固有的}{The work has intrinsic value beyond its monetary worth.}}
{{invade}}{/ɪnˈveɪd/}{入侵；侵犯}{The company invaded the market with a low-cost product.}}
{{investigate}}{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/}{调查；研究}{The agency is investigating the cause of the accident.}}
{{invest}}{/ɪnˈvest/}{投资；投入}{The company invested heavily in research and development.}}
{{invisible}}{/ɪnˈvɪzəbl/}{看不见的；无形的}{The virus is invisible to the naked eye.}}
{{involve}}{/ɪnˈvɒlv/}{涉及；包含}{The job involves a great deal of travel.}}
{{irony}}{/ˈaɪrəni/}{讽刺；反语}{The irony of the situation was not lost on anyone.}}
{{irrelevant}}{/ɪˈreləvənt/}{不相关的；不切题的}{The information is irrelevant to the current discussion.}}
{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}{隔离；孤立}{Scientists isolated the gene responsible for the condition.}}
{{journal}}{/ˈdʒɜːnl/}{期刊；日志}{The research was published in a prestigious medical journal.}}
{{junction}}{/ˈdʒʌŋkʃn/}{交叉点；连接}{The accident occurred at a busy junction.}}
{{jury}}{/ˈdʒʊəri/}{陪审团}{The jury reached a unanimous verdict.}}
{{justice}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪs/}{正义；公正}{The pursuit of justice is a fundamental principle of law.}}
{{keen}}{/kiːn/}{热切的；敏锐的}{She has a keen eye for detail.}}
{{landscape}}{/ˈlændskeɪp/}{景色；格局}{The political landscape has changed dramatically.}}
{{largely}}{/ˈlɑːdʒli/}{在很大程度上}{The success of the project was largely due to teamwork.}}
{{latter}}{/ˈlætər/}{后者的；后面的}{Of the two options, the latter is more practical.}}
